rzas externas. Estas situaciones pueden afectar distintas partes del cuerpo y requieren una intervenci","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintWidth":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintHeight":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":496.6298828125,"ty":4287}}},"id":"406ab9ab-0c14-4b01-b356-01ade522e1af","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1189.4052734375,"ty":-7413},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":916},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":124,"x":0}],[{"y":39,"from":124,"to":246,"x":0}],[{"y":63,"from":246,"to":344,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"El manejo de traumas en la primera infancia reúne las acciones iniciales destinadas a atender lesiones causadas por caídas, golpes, accidentes u otras fuerzas externas. Estas situaciones pueden afectar distintas partes del cuerpo y requieren una intervención oportuna para disminuir el riesgo de agravamiento y prevenir posibles complicaciones."}},{"type":"text","name":"El primer respondiente debe identificar el tipo de trauma, valorar la gravedad de la lesión y actuar de manera segura, priorizando la inmovilización, la protección de la zona afectada y la estabilidad de la niña o del niño. La intervención debe evitar movi","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintWidth":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintHeight":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":289,"ty":4544}}},"id":"a4f9c196-07c3-44e6-8906-b176244360aa","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1397.03515625,"ty":-7156},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":1124},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":153,"x":0}],[{"y":39,"from":153,"to":305,"x":0}],[{"y":63,"from":305,"to":370,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"El primer respondiente debe identificar el tipo de trauma, valorar la gravedad de la lesión y actuar de manera segura, priorizando la inmovilización, la protección de la zona afectada y la estabilidad de la niña o del niño. La intervención debe evitar movimientos innecesarios que puedan agravar el daño, especialmente en casos de compromiso de cabeza, cuello o columna."}},{"type":"text","name":"Para orientar una atención segura, es necesario reconocer las características de la lesión y la zona del cuerpo comprometida. En la primera infancia, los golpes o las caídas pueden afectar especialmente la cabeza y el cuello; por ello, resulta fundamental ","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintHeight":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":185,"ty":4658}}},"id":"2b831dde-24b4-4178-948a-60a6b58f171b","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1501.03515625,"ty":-7042},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":1228},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":174,"x":0}],[{"y":39,"from":174,"to":342,"x":0}],[{"y":63,"from":342,"to":513,"x":0}],[{"y":87,"from":513,"to":536,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"Para orientar una atención segura, es necesario reconocer las características de la lesión y la zona del cuerpo comprometida. En la primera infancia, los golpes o las caídas pueden afectar especialmente la cabeza y el cuello; por ello, resulta fundamental diferenciar los tipos de trauma, reconocer sus signos de alarma y aplicar las medidas iniciales correspondientes, sin realizar movimientos que puedan agravar el daño. Con este propósito, se presentan las características y las medidas de atención inicial de los siguientes traumas:"}},{"type":"text","name":"Debido a las características físicas propias de esta etapa, las niñas y los niños pueden presentar mayor vulnerabilidad ante algunas lesiones. Por ello, la atención debe realizarse con cuidado, evitando movimientos innecesarios y observando permanentemente","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintWidth":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintHeight":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":527.6298828125,"ty":4416}}},"id":"f41361e5-1262-4fd7-b897-74f2cd042cb6","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1158.4052734375,"ty":-7284},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":854},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":120,"x":0}],[{"y":39,"from":120,"to":230,"x":0}],[{"y":63,"from":230,"to":295,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"Debido a las características físicas propias de esta etapa, las niñas y los niños pueden presentar mayor vulnerabilidad ante algunas lesiones. Por ello, la atención debe realizarse con cuidado, evitando movimientos innecesarios y observando permanentemente cualquier cambio en su estado general."}},{"type":"group","name":"Enmascarar grupo 1119277","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_MASK","constraintLeft":true,"constraintWidth":true,"constraintHeight":true,"clipPathResources":{"children":[{"type":"shape","name":"Rectángulo 457003","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_RECTANGLE"}},"id":"22752a6e-d278-49f2-9641-05da43b77c55","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":184.6298828125,"ty":7256},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":142,"g":197,"b":252}}},"stroke":{"type":"none","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":112,"g":112,"b":112}},"width":1,"align":"inside"}},"shape":{"type":"rect","x":0,"y":0,"width":292,"height":227,"r":[1,1,1,1]}}],"type":"clipPath"},"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":0,"ty":-2969}}},"id":"e13571d7-5f52-4d08-85e7-5fe2dd710bd3","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1686.03515625,"ty":-14669},"group":{"children":[{"type":"shape","name":"Imagen 79","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_IMAGE","aspectLock":{"width":500,"height":333}}},"id":"506bc733-177c-4456-b441-82b70c4f406f","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":160.6298828125,"ty":7233.095703125},"style":{"fill":{"type":"pattern","pattern":{"width":500,"height":333,"meta":{"ux":{"scaleBehavior":"fill","uid":"95333b4cc22d15df9f1ca9b1015d9c5a","hrefLastModifiedDate":1785198359}},"href":""}},"stroke":{"type":"none","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":112,"g":112,"b":112}},"width":1,"align":"inside"}},"shape":{"type":"rect","x":0,"y":0,"width":376.55670166015625,"height":250.8087615966797}}]}},{"type":"text","name":"Asimismo, es fundamental valorar el estado general de la niña o del niño, observar la zona afectada y evitar movimientos que puedan agravar la lesión. Esta valoración permite reconocer señales de alarma y determinar la necesidad de recibir atención especia","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintTop":true,"constraintHeight":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":186,"ty":685.5}}},"id":"49706f25-6549-4e34-ab22-0cde3992179e","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1500.03515625,"ty":-11014.5},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":1228},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":167,"x":0}],[{"y":39,"from":167,"to":263,"x":0}]]},{"lines":[[{"y":63,"from":264,"to":264,"x":0}]]},{"lines":[[{"y":87,"from":265,"to":404,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"Asimismo, es fundamental valorar el estado general de la niña o del niño, observar la zona afectada y evitar movimientos que puedan agravar la lesión. Esta valoración permite reconocer señales de alarma y determinar la necesidad de recibir atención especializada.\n\nEstas situaciones pueden presentarse con frecuencia en los entornos cotidianos de la primera infancia. Algunos ejemplos son los siguientes:"}},{"type":"text","name":"Antes de realizar el traslado, es necesario organizar la intervención para evitar improvisaciones. Para ello, se deben tener en cuenta los siguientes aspectos:","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintHeight":true,"constraintBottom":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":186,"ty":9282.9921875}}},"id":"767c8cd6-e616-4eaa-a5f4-c2fc2df84d29","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1500.03515625,"ty":-2417.0078125},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":1228},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":159,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"Antes de realizar el traslado, es necesario organizar la intervención para evitar improvisaciones. Para ello, se deben tener en cuenta los siguientes aspectos:"}},{"type":"text","name":"La técnica seleccionada debe modificarse o suspenderse si durante el recorrido aparecen dificultad para respirar, pérdida de respuesta, dolor intenso, vómito o cambios en la coloración de la piel. En estas situaciones, se debe ubicar a la persona lesionada","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintHeight":true,"constraintBottom":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":186,"ty":10056.9921875}}},"id":"795db566-9a00-4436-b693-90f627e1b1e8","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1500.03515625,"ty":-1643.0078125},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":1228},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":171,"x":0}],[{"y":39,"from":171,"to":348,"x":0}],[{"y":63,"from":348,"to":356,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"La técnica seleccionada debe modificarse o suspenderse si durante el recorrido aparecen dificultad para respirar, pérdida de respuesta, dolor intenso, vómito o cambios en la coloración de la piel. En estas situaciones, se debe ubicar a la persona lesionada en un lugar seguro, solicitar atención especializada y mantener la vigilancia de su estado general."}},{"type":"text","name":"El conocimiento de estas técnicas fortalece la capacidad de respuesta ante lesiones y traumatismos en la primera infancia. Asimismo, permite actuar con mayor seguridad frente a otras situaciones específicas que requieren observación, reconocimiento de sign","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintHeight":true,"constraintBottom":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":186,"ty":10343.9990234375}}},"id":"4494cd60-2452-4072-8749-32fe6261dc34","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1500.03515625,"ty":-1356.0009765625},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":1228},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":168,"x":0}],[{"y":39,"from":168,"to":297,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"El conocimiento de estas técnicas fortalece la capacidad de respuesta ante lesiones y traumatismos en la primera infancia. Asimismo, permite actuar con mayor seguridad frente a otras situaciones específicas que requieren observación, reconocimiento de signos de alarma y atención inicial oportuna."}},{"type":"text","name":"Una vez verificadas estas condiciones, se puede seleccionar la técnica que responda a las características de la situación:","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintHeight":true,"constraintBottom":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":186,"ty":9580}}},"id":"990166dd-33b3-4ac1-9597-6580ccf85ee0","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1500.03515625,"ty":-2120},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":1228},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":122,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"Una vez verificadas estas condiciones, se puede seleccionar la técnica que responda a las características de la situación:"}},{"type":"text","name":"Reconocer estos eventos permite identificar los posibles riesgos y aplicar las medidas iniciales correspondientes. En el siguiente apartado, se presentan las características de las heridas, las hemorragias y las quemaduras, junto con las acciones básicas p","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintTop":true,"constraintHeight":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":186,"ty":1247.6611328125}}},"id":"b16e1185-86a9-43ef-a36d-6b63039fca8c","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1500.03515625,"ty":-10452.3388671875},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":1228},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":174,"x":0}],[{"y":39,"from":174,"to":288,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"Reconocer estos eventos permite identificar los posibles riesgos y aplicar las medidas iniciales correspondientes. En el siguiente apartado, se presentan las características de las heridas, las hemorragias y las quemaduras, junto con las acciones básicas para brindar una atención segura."}},{"type":"text","name":"Las heridas, las hemorragias y las quemaduras pueden afectar la piel y otros tejidos. Reconocer sus características permite brindar una atención inicial segura, prevenir complicaciones y solicitar ayuda especializada cuando sea necesario.\n\nLas principales ","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_GROUP","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintTop":true,"constraintHeight":true,"singleTextObject":true,"rangedStyles":[{"length":1094,"linkId":"","fontFamily":"Roboto","fontStyle":"Regular","postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","fontSize":16,"charSpacing":2.5,"underline":false,"textTransform":"none","textScript":"none","fill":{"value":4279379519},"strikethrough":false,"hyperlinkUrl":""}],"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":186,"ty":1532.6611328125}}},"id":"0fd24b45-0676-4314-98bc-98689d6572cc","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1500.03515625,"ty":-10167.3388671875},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":18,"g":38,"b":63}}},"font":{"postscriptName":"Roboto-Regular","family":"Roboto","style":"Regular","size":16},"textAttributes":{"letterSpacing":2.5,"lineHeight":24}},"text":{"frame":{"type":"autoHeight","width":1228},"paragraphs":[{"lines":[[{"y":15,"from":0,"to":170,"x":0}],[{"y":39,"from":170,"to":238,"x":0}]]},{"lines":[[{"y":63,"from":239,"to":239,"x":0}]]},{"lines":[[{"y":87,"from":240,"to":318,"x":0}]]}],"rawText":"Las heridas, las hemorragias y las quemaduras pueden afectar la piel y otros tejidos. Reconocer sus características permite brindar una atención inicial segura, prevenir complicaciones y solicitar ayuda especializada cuando sea necesario.\n\nLas principales lesiones y sus medidas de atención inicial son las siguientes:"}},{"type":"shape","name":"Rectángulo 456505","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_RECTANGLE","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constraintTop":true,"constraintHeight":true,"localTransform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":290.03515625,"ty":1859}}},"id":"50e896b2-05e7-4f24-a403-d1ec62788755","transform":{"a":1,"b":0,"c":0,"d":1,"tx":-1396,"ty":-9841},"style":{"fill":{"type":"solid","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":184,"g":244,"b":206}}},"stroke":{"type":"none","color":{"mode":"RGB","value":{"r":112,"g":112,"b":112}},"width":1,"align":"inside"}},"shape":{"type":"rect","x":0,"y":0,"width":1020,"height":90,"r":[20,20,20,20]}},{"type":"shape","name":"Rectángulo 457130","meta":{"ux":{"nameL10N":"SHAPE_RECTANGLE","constraintLeft":true,"constraintRight":true,"constrain